- op: discuss  # 048d
  at: '2026-05-30T09:06:43Z'  # 048d
  by: agent  # 048d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 048d
  clock: 4  # 048d
  nonce: 048d  # 048d
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Member candidate for INV-numat — the field is a vocabulary/axis question (derivable vs stored). Sibling to INV-jusot (modifiers): same writer-side pattern of per-emitter ad hoc field population without shared registry — 7 linker files at event_sourcing.py:787, message_queue.py:533, database_query.py:440, websocket.py:888, graphql_resolver.py:521,547, http.py:1500, graphql.py:303 each reinvent `is_cross_language = src.language != dst.language`. dependency-linker, enclosure-linker, html, solidity never added the check, producing the 35-edge undercount (26 of which are depends_on_manifest). cross_language=False on 103 within-language edges is a zero-entropy-when-derivable sub-pattern of INV-lifik §1. Structural fix: either drop the field (derivable from node.language on src/dst) or move to a sketch-build-time post-processing layer that uniformly stamps it — same shape as the access_mode centralization gap in INV-kudug."  # 048d
- op: discuss  # 95f6
  at: '2026-06-02T05:28:04Z'  # 95f6
  by: agent  # 95f6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 95f6
  clock: 5  # 95f6
  nonce: 95f6  # 95f6
  message: "Pass-25 cross-format consistency probe — cross_language meta flag still has false-positives on post-INV-sugat-closure substrate:\n\nF25.16: 27 edges have actually-cross-language endpoints (src.language != dst.language, neither None); 29 edges have meta.cross_language=True flag set. Delta = 2 edges where flag is set but src/dst languages agree. The miss-rate (pass-19 F: meta.cross_language=False on 55% of actual cross-language edges) was not directly re-measured here; pass-25 only computed the over-mark direction.\n\nINV-zigup's original \"misses 55% of actually-cross-language edges\" measurement would need re-running to verify whether the miss-rate has improved post-INV-sugat-closure. The 2-edge over-mark face is small but stable.\n\nSample cross-language disagreement: ('script_src', 'html', 'javascript') — correctly cross-language (HTML embedding JS via <script src>), which IS flagged. So at least one cross-language edge type is correctly handled.\n\nStatus remains violated. The \"over-mark\" face has the opposite sign of INV-zigup's original \"under-mark\" finding, but both point at the same axis-mixing root: the flag isn't derived from a canonical rule like `src.language != dst.language`, but from per-emitter heuristics that may set it inconsistently."  # 95f6
- op: discuss  # dffc
  at: '2026-06-07T03:11:53Z'  # dffc
  by: agent  # dffc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dffc
  clock: 6  # dffc
  nonce: dffc  # dffc
  message: "Re-confirmed + converse-facet on fresh substrate (dogfood_tranche_07 F126.A2, cluster C2; F122.A3, F127.A2 facets): all 29 cross_language=True edges are incident to a language=None synthetic node — ('typescript','None','calls') x12 (websocket-linker WS edges, dst /ws-endpoint:function has node.language=None even though the path came from a Python file) and ('None','sql','references') x17 (database-query-linker; src synthetic call_site language=None). So a consumer CANNOT graph-verify cross-language-ness: one of src.lang/dst.lang is always None. This row names the under-mark (55% miss); this is the converse — the flagged-true set is graph-unverifiable because the source language never survives into the synthetic node. Also: F122.A3 (130 function/method nodes language=None all have signature=None) + F127.A2 (synthetic event_subscriber nodes language=None) propagate the same root."  # dffc
